# GRIDLAB

GRIDLAB is an interactive Formula 1 season dashboard built entirely with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

It is designed as a lightweight, animated F1 experience that can be deployed directly through GitHub Pages without requiring a backend, database, authentication system, or build process.

## Features

- Current Formula 1 driver standings
- Constructor standings
- Current and upcoming race information
- Full season calendar
- Previous race results
- Current Formula 1 driver grid
- Real driver photographs
- Animated driver cards
- Click-to-flip driver cards with additional statistics and information
- Current constructor and car gallery
- Animated car movement and racing effects on hover
- Click-to-flip constructor cards with additional team and car information
- Team-specific colours and visual styling
- Pit Wall race prediction system
- Predictions stored locally using `localStorage`
- Live public F1 data fetching with built-in fallback data
- Responsive desktop, tablet, and mobile layouts
- Futuristic motorsport-inspired typography and interface
- Animated race-control backgrounds and micro-interactions
- Reduced-motion accessibility support
- Single-file architecture using only `index.html`

## Technology

- HTML5
- CSS3
- Vanilla JavaScript
- LocalStorage
- Public Formula 1 data sources
- GitHub Pages

No frameworks, server, database, API keys, or package installation are required.

## Deployment

1. Create a GitHub repository.
2. Upload `index.html` to the root of the repository.
3. Open **Settings > Pages**.
4. Select **Deploy from a branch**.
5. Select the `main` branch and `/root`.
6. Save the configuration.

The website can then run directly through GitHub Pages.

## Project Goal

The project explores how a completely static website can still provide a rich, interactive and visually engaging Formula 1 experience through browser-side JavaScript, public motorsport data, animation, responsive design, and local storage.

## P.S.

This project was built through AI-assisted vibe coding, guided by my own creativity, ideas, and basic understanding of development. It was an experimental project focused on exploring what’s possible through AI-powered development.
